181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (My main recommendation is to establish a shared reference for game states, decision dependencies, scene transitions, and scoring rules before implementing the interface.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (Each scene should have a clearly defined trigger, required information, and expected next step. When a decision is changed, the team should also review all subsequent rounds that depend on it.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (I would also recommend maintaining one primary development version instead of allowing the frontend and backend to evolve into separate products.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (Finally, although AI coding tools can accelerate development, they are most effective when developers understand the intended behavior, provide precise requirements, and verify the resulting implementation against the actual player journey.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
